  grow-from-root-default: make defaulting bart2's init to the XBART
    grow-from-root warm start a LIVE OPTION (VD 2026-08-08; the landed
    surface is n.grow.sweeps = 0L opt-in, docs/plans/grow-from-root-
    warm-start.md). Prerequisites before the flip is decidable:
    (1) categorical support in the scan/grower - v1 is ordinal-only and
    never splits categorical predictors, a silent init bias for
    categorical-heavy designs if defaulted; (2) a measured default k
    (early-iteration RMSE / effective burn-in vs k, a few n and signal
    regimes; the method default 2L is unmeasured); (3) family
    consistency - the multinomial/rbart bart2 branches refuse
    n.grow.sweeps today (R/bart.R:470-490), so the default either
    extends there or the difference is documented. The flip itself is a
    draw-law change on the default path: every equivalence baseline and
    hard-coded snapshot re-records in the same battery. Posterior is
    invariant (warm-start only), so the decision is init quality +
    surface economics, not correctness.
  integer-predictor-storage: dense-INTEGER storage in the
    PredictorSource view. denseValues is const double* (data.hpp ~188),
    ColumnType is semantic only (ordinal | categorical), and R still
    as.doubles at the bartcore.R entrances. A memory win, not speed;
    integer -> double is exact in range so the slice MUST be
    trio-bitwise. Split out of typed-ingestion at its 2026-08-06
    close: the typing that mattered (ordinal vs categorical with
    declared K) landed with slice 2b; storage width is a separate
    question with its own gate. consumer-gated.
